    <briefdescription>
<para>Owns application startup: configuration, banner, Drogon wiring, and post-run executor shutdown. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The constructor resolves long-lived singletons from the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref> and copies the server and database configuration by value, so later changes to the <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref> are not seen through those copies. <ref refid="classServer_1a30362b937b125d27916cf595bfc4c1a7" kindref="member">run()</ref> configures and starts the Drogon application, installs the pre-routing and pre-sending advice (method filtering and CORS), and blocks until the event loops stop. Only then does it shut the worker pools down, while the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref> singletons they depend on are still alive. The filter and middleware members are created eagerly so one instance is reused. Registration of the included Drogon components (including the route headers brought in by <ref refid="all__routes_8hpp" kindref="compound">all_routes.hpp</ref>) is handled by Drogon itself, outside this class. <simplesect kind="note"><para>Not copyable. Move construction is defaulted; move assignment is deleted. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="namespaceCors" kindref="compound">Cors</ref>, <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>, <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
